# Comments and JSDoc

Comments, test names, and JSDoc are written in English. Identifiers stay in English.

Each module starts with the existing file header:

```typescript
/**
 * @file chessTypes.ts
 * @project w3dts
 * @author Cyril TARRIET
 * @description Shared chess square and piece types for rules and spawn.
 */
```

Document exported functions, classes, and non-obvious types. State the contract, not the implementation steps.

```typescript
/**
 * Maps a square name to the center of that square on the board.
 * @param square - File and rank, such as `e4`.
 * @param y - Height in metres. Defaults to the board surface.
 * @returns World position in metres.
 */
export function squareToWorld(square: ChessSquareName, y?: number): vec3
```

Mark symbols that must stay out of the published API with `@internal`. Do not document private helpers whose names already state the contract.

`pnpm run docs` runs TypeDoc on `src/chess/index.ts`. `pnpm docs` is the npm page opener, not this script. CI fails if generation fails.
